Subject: [PATCH 21/21] fix(asks): four holes in the thank-you, found in review
 before it ships (1692)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. A „helped" on an ask nobody answered (the no-answer debrief records
   worked=true when it was solved elsewhere) offered to thank that person,
   and a yes sent „Nino says thank you for your help" to someone who never
   helped. The card now needs an answered, not declined, ask.
2. „კი, მადლობა გადაუხადე" arriving twice in a second (the repo's row 115
   shape) thanked the helper and the chain twice. The card is claimed with
   a conditional UPDATE … RETURNING before anything is sent; the second tap
   finds it taken. The „ask again?" step is claimed the same way.
3. The Georgian no-label „არა, საჭირო არაა" was the match card's (1699) too,
   and the match tap runs first — a tap could settle the wrong card. Now
   „არა, მადლობა არ მინდა"; every thanks label is unique in services.
4. A day-14 „following up" row blocked the card if the owner said it helped
   later. Such a row now gives way to the card (ON CONFLICT … WHERE state =
   'followed_up').

Not yet: a „not yet" on the held answer debrief re-arms the old kind; it
comes with AV.

